Worked example:

```javascript
function hasDuplicateIds(notes) {
  const ids=notes.map(note=>note.id);
  return new Set(ids).size !== ids.length;
}
console.log(hasDuplicateIds([{"id":1},{"id":2}]));
```
The returned value is false.

after:
```javascript
function hasDuplicateIds(notes) {
  const ids=notes.map(note=>note.id);
  return new Set(ids).size !== ids.length;
}
console.log(hasDuplicateIds([{"id":1},{"id":2}]));
```
This prints false. IDs 1 and 2 are different, so neither is repeated.
